From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp: Give the camera clock controller its MX domain

The camera PLLs run on MX (see the camcc-sc8280xp change): list MX as
the second power domain of the camera clock controller, at SVS_L1, the
level its 1116 MHz PLL needs, with MMCX at LOW_SVS as before.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi
index 1b2d9cdd4..c9ebcd061 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi
@@ -4722,8 +4722,10 @@ camcc: clock-controller@ad00000 {
 				 <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK>,
 				 <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK_A>,
 				 <&sleep_clk>;
-			power-domains = <&rpmhpd SC8280XP_MMCX>;
-			required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_low_svs>;
+			power-domains = <&rpmhpd SC8280XP_MMCX>,
+					<&rpmhpd SC8280XP_MX>;
+			required-opps = <&rpmhpd_opp_low_svs>,
+					<&rpmhpd_opp_svs_l1>;
 			#clock-cells = <1>;
 			#reset-cells = <1>;
 			#power-domain-cells = <1>;
